Disable SSH ControlMaster multiplexing for Windows hostagent commands.

On Windows, bundled and system Win32-OpenSSH clients fail immediately with
getsockname failed: Not a socket when ControlMaster/ControlPath options are
present while executing a remote command. Both streamCloudInitLog and
probeCloudInitCompleted passed .sshConfig.Args() directly, causing
first-boot cloud-init progress monitoring to fail every stream/probe attempt
and stall for the full 10-minute idle timeout (cloud-init did not report
completion: no boot progress for 10m0s) even after guest provisioning and
/run/lima-boot-done had already completed.

Strip ControlMaster/ControlPath/ControlPersist on Windows across hostagent's
command-executing SSH helpers (streamCloudInitLog, probeCloudInitCompleted,
executeSSH, copyToHost, and ForwardAgent), honor .sshExe, hide
background console windows on Windows, and include bounded stderr in
cloud-init log stream errors.
